                <pb facs="0620" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/8037</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-21">May 21, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your despatch No. 192 of May
                    4, 1934, concerning the political situation in Nicaragua, the Department
                    approves of your interpretation of its policy as set forth in the penultimate
                    paragraph thereof.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
